      "narrative": "Pinal County’s median asking price was $385,000 in September 2026, down 2.53% year over year, while the median sale price was $371,514, down 1.1% year over year and 2.2% from the prior month.[1][3] Inventory stood at 2,657 homes for sale, up 11% year over year, with 3.5 months of supply and homes averaging 77 days on market.[1][3] The pending ratio of 0.3448 indicates that a relatively large share of listed homes was already under contract, but increased inventory and buyer concessions point to greater buyer leverage.[1][2] Active construction by Pulte and D.R. Horton around Queen Creek and San Tan Valley, along with continued migration from Maricopa County and growth along the I-10 and SR 347 corridors, are notable local drivers.[2][7]",
